# Regression pin for #1417: a string whose text is a YAML scalar of another type must be QUOTED
# on dump, or it changes type on the way back in. `safe_dump("true")` emitted the bare scalar
# `true`, which `safe_load` then read as the BOOLEAN — silent type corruption across a
# serialization boundary. PyYAML quotes all of these, and now so does Sharpy.
#
# The rule is asked of YamlScalarResolver, the same authority safe_load resolves through, so the
# two directions cannot disagree by construction.
#
# The obvious control — that `hello` stays BARE, gaining nothing — cannot live in this fixture
# until #1348 lands. This fixture is compared against CPython by the differential oracle, and
# PyYAML terminates a PLAIN scalar document with the `...` marker that Sharpy does not yet emit:
# CPython prints `hello\n...` where Sharpy prints `hello`, so the control would fail here on
# #1348's account rather than this one's. It lives in stdlib_yaml_round_trip instead, which
# compares loaded VALUES and is therefore immune to document-marker differences. Move it here
# once #1348 lands and both arms agree.
import yaml

def main():
    print(yaml.safe_dump("true").strip())
    print(yaml.safe_dump("42").strip())
